  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday) \nIssued at 1002 PM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nOne more round of isolated storms is possible Saturday afternoon and \nevening near the TX/NM state line before the building upper level \nridge cuts off our supply of monsoonal moisture. Models remain in \ngood agreement keeping ridging firmly in place through early next \nweek with high temperatures expected to remain in the range of about \n5 to 10 degrees above normal, though at this time it appears that \nhighs will remain below record levels. Model spread still increases \nheading into the second half of the week with the precise evolution \nof the riding aloft remaining uncertain. Even so, it looks unlikely \nthat any meaningful moisture will be able to move over the West TX \nregion, and the large majority of ensemble members maintain a dry \nand anomalously warm forecast through the end of the week.",
